<http://data.silknow.org/object/b13da73b-52d9-377c-a791-fe2f60e029f0>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Unidentified pastoral subject. Right and left selvedges intact, both have blue warp threads. No seams or hems. Cotton printed by copper plate, sepia color. Repeat shows two scenes framed by trees and ground foliage: a group of young people dancing and a family group leaving their thatched-roof house. Stain upper middle; three repairs on left half; several small holes; upper right corner patched with matching chintz."@en ;
